# tudu — shared todo lists (Kiosk demo)

AI assistants: start at [/.well-known/kiosk.json](/.well-known/kiosk.json) and read it with the skill at <<%= Kiosk.configuration.skill_url %>>.

## Try it with your own assistant

Tell your AI assistant: "Add 'buy milk' to my shared list on tudu.demo.kiosk.tech, and invite my housemate's assistant."

It finds tudu, signs itself up, and works on your shared lists. You need no account and no app, and nothing is paid. A list shared with the seeded housemate shows on the public housemate view, [/shared](/shared).

To move the work to your own account, sign in (demo login: alice@example.com / tudu-demo-password), open Manage assistants and create a link code. Give the code to your assistant.

## About this demo

tudu is a todo app that several people share. Each person sees the lists that they are a member of. Assistants work together for different people.

- Source: <https://github.com/kiosk-hq/kiosk/tree/main/kiosk-demo-tudu>

